<http://data.silknow.org/object/2ecaafe7-10af-3224-a6fb-ccddc6e7a719>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "'Berhampore silk', whether raw or manufactured, referred to products from four different local centres which were marketed at Berhampore (modern Baharampur); it was then a substantial industry. Tie-dyeing and its printed imitations are no longer produced in West Bengal. In 1882, this sari was probably resist-dyed."@en , "Sari. Berhampore, ca. 1880."@en , "Silk sari printed in imitation of tie-dye with small white spots on a blue ground forming a trellis in the centre; and broad border of boteh."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/5e7abe2c-811a-3d40-af2c-8a4165de155e> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/007cd34d-bfa8-381c-bc19-85a665651994> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "'Berhampore silk', whether raw or manufactured, referred to products from four different local centres which were marketed at Berhampore (modern Baharampur); it was then a substantial industry. Tie-dyeing and its printed imitations are no longer produced in West Bengal. In 1882, this sari was probably resist-dyed."@en , "Silk sari printed in imitation of tie-dye with small white spots on a blue ground forming a trellis in the centre; and broad border of boteh."@en , "Sari. Berhampore, ca. 1880."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/2ecaafe7-10af-3224-a6fb-ccddc6e7a719/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/2ecaafe7-10af-3224-a6fb-ccddc6e7a719/dimension/2> ;
